{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YV6AWbXRP1Ru9FY4DjqR1u","type":"tool_result","content":"18:## [1.4.4] - 2026-11-03\n493:## [1.4.3] - 2026-10-15\n1043:## [1.4.2] - 2026-09-25\n1045:Express release (PLAN-193). Claude Opus 5.5 (`claude-opus-5-5`) becomes the\n1048:upgraded install whose shipped Opus 5 pin moves to Opus 5.5, and whose\n1050:default, instead of medium, the Opus 5.5 one. **Claude Code 2.1.280 or later\n1064:### Changed — Claude Opus 5.5 is the session default and joins the VETO floor (PLAN-193, ADR-149 Amendment 3)\n1066:- `claude-opus-5-5` is appended at the END of the ADR-149 working set, and so\n1073:- **VETO floor.** `claude-opus-5-5` joins the ids an agent file with\n1085:  a model up by its exact spelling does not price the `claude-opus-5-5[1m]`\n1107:  of `claude-opus-5-5[1m]` as the allowlisted `claude-opus-5-5`: one trailing\n1122:  `availableModels` is written with the list that has `claude-opus-5-5`\n1125:  `model` pin moves to `claude-opus-5-5` when it is absent or is the\n1127:  `availableModels` names `claude-opus-5-5` exactly (Claude Code admits an\n1130:  warning. Opus 5.5 runs at MEDIUM effort when nothing sets a level, where\n1136:  in user settings, which applied to Opus 5, does not apply to Opus 5.5. A\n1138:  nothing else sets a level, Opus 5.5 then runs at its default, medium. An\n1159:- Claude Code added Claude Opus 5.5 in 2.1.280, and 2.1.280 is the minimum\n1422:  The pin (`claude-opus-5-5`) and `fallbackModel` (`claude-opus-5`) are now\n1426:  for what its cache lost meanwhile), runs without the Opus 5.5 thinking\n1510:- After `upgrade.sh`, a pin the framework shipped moves to `claude-opus-5-5`\n1528:## [1.4.1] - 2026-09-18\n1705:## [1.4.0] - 2026-09-07\n2109:## [1.3.0] - 2026-08-04\n2352:## [1.2.0] - 2026-07-30\n2446:## [1.1.0] - 2026-07-13\n2532:## [1.0.1] - 2026-07-02\n2634:## [1.0.0] — 2026-06-29"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dbb97fe8-0e18-4c56-9a57-e9a508557997","uuid"